    "body": "@caridy events have four phases: none, capturing, at target, and bubbling. Capturing and at target are always performed. If we did not perform at target for a composed event, it would actually leak that there was a component as the target for an event we could observe during capturing was not in our tree. (I realize this is the opposite of what you suggest, but it's unclear to me how you're arriving at your conclusion.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
